<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 44,820 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 44,820 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust  said it had handled 44,820 tonnes of export and import cargo in the  24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 62,410 tonnes  in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	July 31</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 9,650	12,764</p>
<p>    Import cargo		35,170	49,646</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and two berthed. In the next  24 hours, two are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.   </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload  at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     30,000	 Iliad		     1/8</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     42,000	 Trade Resolve	   2/8</p>
<p>High speed diesel  70,000	 Chesapeak City	  4/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
